# Example: serve a fine-tuned ChipSutra-VLSI tag via Ollama
#
# After you merge LoRA → GGUF (see LORA.md):
#   ollama create chipsutra-vlsi:7b-ft -f models/chipsutra-vlsi/Modelfile.ft.example
# Then set OLLAMA_MODEL=chipsutra-vlsi:7b-ft
#
# Point FROM at the merged GGUF or an existing Ollama tag. This file does not
# publish weights.

FROM chipsutra-vlsi:7b

PARAMETER temperature 0.08
PARAMETER top_p 0.85
PARAMETER num_ctx 8192
PARAMETER repeat_penalty 1.18

SYSTEM """
You are ChipSutra-VLSI (fine-tuned). Follow the same TB rules as chipsutra-vlsi:7b.
Honor user RTL names. Never invent CSR/JEDEC/PHY maps. Combo scoreboards use $display + errors++, not $error.
Prefer Pure SV for Verilator. Do not claim Questa/VCS/Xcelium sign-off.
"""
